---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { COMPANY, PLANS, RELEASE, TRIAL, pageFor } from '../data/site';
import { lastModified } from '../lib/lastmod';

// How-to for the memory app. Every step quotes the app's own screens and
// buttons (crates/vault-tauri/dist/index.html and app.js, read in session 63),
// so a label renamed there must be renamed here too. Only apps that passed a
// live test get connection steps (VERIFIED_APPS in data/site.ts).
const page = pageFor('/docs/');
const win = RELEASE.windows;
const updated = lastModified(page.sources);
const updatedLabel = updated
  ? new Date(updated).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })
  : undefined;
---
<Base page={page}>
  <section class="page doc">
    <h1>Documents</h1>
    <p>How to install the Zaaheen memory app, connect your AI apps to it, and look after your
       memories. Each step uses the same words you will see on screen.</p>
    {updatedLabel && <p class="doc-updated">Last updated {updatedLabel}</p>}

    <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#install">Installing Zaaheen</a></li>
        <li><a href="#first-launch">The first time you open it</a></li>
        <li><a href="#connect">Connecting your AI apps</a></li>
        <li><a href="#location">Where your memories are kept</a></li>
        <li><a href="#consolidation">Keeping your memory tidy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#download">Taking your memories with you</a></li>
        <li><a href="#delete">Deleting everything</a></li>
        <li><a href="#subscription">Your trial and subscription</a></li>
        <li><a href="#uninstall">Uninstalling</a></li>
        <li><a href="#help">Getting help</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="install">How to install Zaaheen</h2>
    {!RELEASE.available && <p><strong>Zaaheen for Windows is coming soon.</strong> These steps
       are how it works once you can download it.</p>}
    <p>Download the installer for Windows ({win.arch}{RELEASE.available ? `, ${win.size}` : ''}) and open it. Zaaheen
       {RELEASE.version} is a {RELEASE.stage.toLowerCase()} and has been tested on
       {win.tested}. It is not available for macOS or Linux yet.</p>
    <p>Two things happen while it installs:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Windows says the publisher is unknown.</strong> We are a small company and have
          not bought a code-signing certificate yet. Choose <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run
          anyway</em>.</li>
      <li><strong>Windows asks for administrator permission.</strong> Zaaheen installs for
          everyone on the computer, so Windows asks once. It does not need administrator rights
          to run afterwards.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="first-launch">What happens the first time you open it</h2>
    <p>Choose <em>Begin set up</em>. Setting up takes about three minutes:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Your account.</strong> Choose <em>Create an account</em> or <em>Sign in</em>.
          This opens your web browser. Your {TRIAL.days}-day free trial starts when you create
          your account, and no card is needed. Signing in never shares your memories with us.</li>
      <li><strong>Where to keep your memories.</strong> The usual place suits most people. You
          can change it later.</li>
      <li><strong>Your first AI app.</strong> Pick the app you use and follow the steps, or choose
          <em>I'll connect one later</em>.</li>
      <li><strong>Your first memory.</strong> Tell Zaaheen something your AI apps should know
          about you, then choose <em>Keep this memory</em>, or <em>Skip for now</em>.</li>
      <li><strong>Tidying up.</strong> Choose whether Zaaheen keeps your memory tidy on its own
          each day, then <em>Finish setup</em>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The first time, Zaaheen also downloads what it needs to search your memories. It does this
       in the background, and you can use it while it finishes.</p>

    <h2 id="connect">How to connect your AI apps</h2>
    <p>Open the <em>Agents</em> tab and choose <em>+ Connect an AI app</em>. Zaaheen never changes
       another app's settings itself: it hands the app what it needs, and the app asks you.</p>
    <h3>Claude (the app for your computer)</h3>
    <p>Choose <em>Connect it for me</em>. Claude asks you to install Zaaheen: click
       <em>Install</em>, and it's connected. It works in Claude's Chat and Cowork. If Claude does
       not ask, Zaaheen saves the extension to your Downloads folder: in Claude, open Settings,
       then Extensions, then Advanced settings, then Install Extension, and choose
       "Zaaheen for Claude.mcpb".</p>
    <h3>Cursor</h3>
    <p>Choose <em>Connect it for me</em>. Cursor asks you to install Zaaheen: click
       <em>Install</em>, and it's connected.</p>
    <h3>ChatGPT (the app for your computer)</h3>
    <p>In ChatGPT, open Settings, then Integrations, then Plugins. Choose Add, then Add MCP Server,
       and fill it in:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Name: <code>Zaaheen</code></li>
      <li>Command: <code>zaaheen</code></li>
      <li>Arguments: <code>mcp</code> and <code>serve</code>, as two separate items</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Save it, then use Zaaheen in ChatGPT's Work or Codex mode. Its Chat mode cannot connect to
       apps on your computer.</p>
    <h3>Other AI apps</h3>
    <p>Zaaheen connects over MCP, the standard many AI apps use. The <em>Agents</em> tab shows the
       setting for other apps too. An app shows in that tab while it is open and connected.</p>

    <h2 id="location">Where your memories are kept</h2>
    <p>On your own computer, encrypted. They are never uploaded. To keep them in another folder
       or on another drive, open Settings, then <em>Your memories</em>, and choose <em>Move my
       memories…</em>. Zaaheen closes, moves them, and opens again by itself. If it closes
       part-way, your memories stay safe where they were.</p>

    <h2 id="consolidation">What tidying up (consolidation) does</h2>
    <p>While you're away, Zaaheen organises what it has learned: it merges near-duplicates into
       one, resolves facts that contradict each other in favour of the newer one, and archives
       older memories you never use out of everyday recall. It never deletes them, and all of it
       happens on your computer.</p>
    <p>It is off unless you turn it on. In the <em>Consolidation</em> tab, switch on <em>Keep my
       vault tidy automatically</em> and choose every day or once a week, and a time. If your
       computer was asleep or off at that time, it catches up later. To tidy straight away,
       choose <em>Run consolidation now</em>. The first time you turn it on, Zaaheen makes a
       one-time download of about 2.5 GB.</p>

    <h2 id="download">How to take your memories with you</h2>
    <p>Open Settings, then <em>Your memories</em>, and choose <em>Download my memories</em>. It
       saves everything you've kept as one file. It's yours, whether or not you subscribe: the
       button stays available even after a trial or subscription ends.</p>

    <h2 id="delete">How to delete everything</h2>
    <p>Open Settings, then <em>Your memories</em>, and choose <em>Delete everything</em>. Type
       DELETE to confirm, then choose <em>Permanently delete everything</em>. This destroys the
       encryption key and the files, so it cannot be undone or recovered from a copy. Deleting
       your memories does not cancel your subscription; cancel that separately with <em>Manage
       subscription</em>.</p>

    <h2 id="subscription">How the trial and subscription work</h2>
    <p>The first {TRIAL.days} days are free, with no card. After that it is {PLANS.monthly} or
       {PLANS.yearly}. To subscribe, choose <em>Subscribe</em> in the app: payment opens in your browser,
       and Zaaheen unlocks by itself once it goes through. To change your plan, update your card
       or cancel, open Settings, then Account, and choose <em>Manage subscription</em>.</p>
    <p>If a trial or subscription ends, nothing is deleted. Everything stays on your computer,
       and you can still download it.</p>

    <h2 id="uninstall">How to uninstall Zaaheen</h2>
    <p>Use Windows Settings, then Apps, then Installed apps, and uninstall Zaaheen. Uninstalling
       removes the app, not your memories, so reinstalling finds them again. To remove your
       memories as well, use <em>Delete everything</em> first.</p>

    <h2 id="help">How to get help</h2>
    <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a>. If something went wrong, open
       Settings, then Help, and choose <em>Save activity record…</em>, then attach the file. The
       record contains none of your memories.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
